hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24077","Narrated to us Abd al-Razzaq, informed to us Mamar, from al-Zuhri, informed to me Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from Harithah ibn al-Numan, he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him was Jibril, peace be upon him, sitting in the seats. So I greeted him, then I passed. When I returned and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left, he said: Did you see the one who was with me? I said: Yes. He said: He is Jibril, and he returned your greeting."
"24078","Narrated to us Abu Said, narrated to us Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal, he said: I heard Umar, freedman of Ghufrah, narrate from Thalabah ibn Abi Malik, from Harithah ibn al-Numan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you takes grazing livestock and attends prayer in congregation, then his livestock becomes difficult for him, so he says: If I sought for my livestock a place more fertile than this. So he moves, and attends only Friday. Then his livestock becomes difficult for him, so he says: If I sought for my livestock a place more fertile than this. So he moves, and attends neither Friday nor congregation. So his heart is sealed."
